  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 302 PM MST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nBy Friday, the band of elevated 500mb vorticity, should have \nfiltered out of the area, leaving us with ridging aloft. It may\nbe possible for westerly flow, combined with modest humidity, \nto produce orographic precipitation on the windward side of the \nhigher terrain, especially the central mountains, in the \nafternoon. For the rest of the area, expect a dry, partly cloudy\nday.\n\nMoving into this weekend, we will enter a ridging pattern, with\ntemperatures slightly above average, with mostly sunny \nconditions and light winds. The next chance of widespread rain \nlooks to be, at the earliest, Wednesday of next week.",
